"><div><strong>19,272</strong><span>last 7 days</span></div><div><strong>114,212</strong><span>last 28 days</span></div><div><strong>3,446</strong><span>7-day peak</span></div><div><strong>23,705</strong><span>period peak</span></div></div><a class="candidate-source-link" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marine_Le_Pen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Wikipedia article ↗</a></div></article>\n        <article class="candidate-panel candidate-chart-panel"><div class="candidate-panel-head"><div class="candidate-panel-title-row"><h3>PAGEVIEW HISTORY</h3><span class="candidate-section-info-wrap candidate-panel-info-wrap"><button class="candidate-section-info" type="button" aria-label="Pageview history information" aria-describedby="attention-history-note">i</button><span class="candidate-section-tooltip" id="attention-history-note" role="tooltip">Daily pageviews of the French-language Wikipedia article. Repeat visits may be included.</span></span></div><span>90 days</span></div><div class="candidate-panel-body"><div class="candidate-chart" data-chart="attention-history" role="img" aria-label="Daily pageviews of Marine Le Pen&#x27;s French Wikipedia article"><p class="candidate-chart-fallback">History from 13 Aug 2026 to 10 Nov 2026.</p></div></div></article>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n    <section class="candidate-section candidate-public-signals" id="public-signals" aria-labelledby="public-signals-title"><header class="candidate-section-head"><div class="candidate-section-title-row"><h2 id="public-signals-title">PUBLIC SIGNALS</h2><span class="candidate-section-info-wrap"><button class="candidate-section-info" type="button" aria-label="Public signals information" aria-describedby="public-signals-note">i</button><span class="candidate-section-tooltip" id="public-signals-note" role="tooltip">These indicators come from independent sources and do not measure the same thing. They are neither a popularity score nor voting intention.</span></span></div></header><div class="candidate-public-signals-grid"><article class="candidate-panel candidate-public-signal" data-provider="polymarket" data-state="observed" aria-labelledby="polymarket-label"><header class="candidate-panel-head"><div class="candidate-panel-title-row"><h3 id="polymarket-label">Polymarket</h3><span class="candidate-section-info-wrap candidate-panel-info-wrap"><button class="candidate-section-info" type="button" aria-label="Method and provenance — Polymarket" aria-describedby="public-signal-polymarket-note">i</button><span class="candidate-section-tooltip" id="public-signal-polymarket-note" role="tooltip">Election winner, including any runoff. Prediction market — not voting intention and not an FR27 forecast. Third-party value, not calculated by FR27. Participants are not a representative sample of French voters. Liquidity and trading conditions may influence prices. FR27 does not combine this signal with polling, Wikipedia, media, agenda or other evidence into a synthetic score. Absence does not mean 0%. Change compares the current value with the latest valid observation at or before seven days earlier. Insufficient history produces no change or chart. Change in percentage points. Up to 30 days of actual time-spaced observations; missing UTC dates break the line, short runs use dots, the current value is ringed. Sparse coverage hides the chart, not the change. Vertical scale spans at least 5 percentage points. Each chart has its own scale: shapes cannot be compared across platforms.<br><br><span>FR27 observation : <time datetime="2026-11-11T18:04:09.401092Z">11 Nov 2026 18:04 UTC</time>. <span data-polymarket-freshness data-observed-at="2026-11-11T18:04:09.401092Z" data-stale-after-hours="48" aria-live="polite">Check freshness (48h)</span></span></span></span></div></header><div class="candidate-panel-body"><p class="candidate-public-signal-subtitle">Prediction market</p><p class="candidate-public-signal-value"><strong>46.4%</strong></p><p class="candidate-public-signal-unit">Implied probability</p><p class="candidate-public-signal-change"><span aria-hidden="true">+6.2 pts · 7d</span><span class="visually-hidden">Seven-day change: plus 6.2 percentage points in implied probability.</span></p><svg class="candidate-public-signal-trend" viewBox="0 0 240 44" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="Up to 30-day trend in Polymarket implied probability. Seven-day change: plus 6.2 percentage points in implied probability." focusable="false"><g aria-hidden="true"><circle class="candidate-public-signal-trend-point" cx="4.00" cy="30.70" r="1.5"/><circle class="candidate-public-signal-trend-point" cx="11.80" cy="25.89" r="1.5"/><circle class="candidate-public-signal-trend-point" cx="27.39" cy="10.33" r="1.5"/><circle class="candidate-public-signal-trend-point" cx="36.59" cy="15.89" r="1.5"/><circle class="candidate-public-signal-trend-point" cx="50.79" cy="7.00" r="1.5"/><polyline class="candidate-chart-line" points="63.58,15.52 71.61,13.85 79.27,14.41 87.01,14.59 94.57,14.59 102.40,22.93 110.89,23.67 118.43,17.74 126.58,26.63 134.32,27.00 142.03,28.67 149.57,34.04 157.65,35.89 166.62,36.44 173.64,37.00 181.50,36.63 189.29,27.74 196.93,20.70 204.35,18.48 212.21,18.85 221.40,18.11 228.47,18.11 236.00,14.04"/><circle class="candidate-chart-point candidate-public-signal-current" cx="236.00" cy="14.04" r="2.2"/></g></svg><a class="candidate-source-link" href="https://polymarket.com/event/next-french-presidential-election/will-marine-le-pen-win-the-2027-french-presidential-election" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Polymarket ↗</a></div></article><article class="candidate-panel candidate-public-signal" data-provider="youtube" data-state="observed" aria-labelledby="public-signal-youtube-title"><header class="candidate-panel-head"><div class="candidate-panel-title-row"><h3 id="public-signal-youtube-title">YouTube</h3><span class="candidate-section-info-wrap candidate-panel-info-wrap"><button class="candida